@packages/compiler/src/report-protocol.sigil import { SigilCompilationReportProtocol }

component SigilCompilationReportMarkdown {
  goal {
    Give every compiler host one deterministic, agent-readable Markdown projection
    of a completed authoritative CompilationReport.
  }

  interface {
    CompilationReportMarkdown {
      render(CompilationReport) returns one complete Markdown projection without
      changing the report, compilation status, lifecycle, or event delivery

      the projection contains one final status summary, one Stage execution table
      with stage, state, and diagnostic count, then Findings grouped by originating
      stage

      each nonempty stage group has one compact diagnostic table with severity,
      lifecycle, rule code, semantic subject, and location; evidence, impact, and
      suggested correction appear once below the corresponding diagnostic
    }
  }
}

expand SigilCompilationReportMarkdown {
  logic {
    CompilationReportMarkdown {
      Derive every displayed field from the completed CompilationReport, preserve
      report and stage ordering, omit empty sections, and escape report content so it
      cannot change the projection's Markdown structure.

      Render one final report rather than replaying CompilationEvent values or
      repeating the complete JSON representation. Limit ordinary headings to three
      levels.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    CompilationReportMarkdown {
      JSON remains the authoritative durable CompilationReport representation.
      Markdown is a read-only projection and cannot become an input to report
      construction, status calculation, diagnostic identity, lifecycle comparison, or
      event settlement.

      Equivalent decoded CompilationReport values produce byte-identical Markdown
      independent of the calling host.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    CompilerOwnedReportProjection {
      Decision: Own the completed-report Markdown projection in SigilCompiler and
      expose it to every host as one deterministic renderer.

      Scope: Governs Markdown projection of CompilationReport; excludes CLI option
      parsing, terminal progress, and non-compilation workspace Markdown.

      Trade-offs: The compiler package owns a human-readable representation in
      addition to its authoritative JSON schema, so projection changes require
      compiler compatibility review even though they do not change report data. The
      compact Markdown projection intentionally omits report metadata that is not
      needed for immediate review; the authoritative JSON report retains the complete
      data.

      Design issues addressed: One-shot compilation, reusable sessions, CLI export,
      editors, and future hosts must not independently define or drift the final
      report shape.

      Discarded alternatives: CLI-owned rendering duplicates report semantics at one
      host boundary, while exporter-owned rendering prevents non-file consumers from
      reusing the same projection.

      Consequences: Hosts select where to present or persist the projection, while
      SigilCompiler alone determines its content and ordering.
    }
  }

  cases {
    CompilationReportMarkdown {
      A report without current diagnostics renders its status and complete Stage
      execution table and omits Findings.

      A report with findings groups each diagnostic under its originating stage and
      emits its evidence, impact, and correction exactly once.
    }
  }
}
